00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
I'd like to welcome all of you and each of you to Spertus College. I'm Byron Sherwin, the Vice President of Spertus College.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
And I want first of all to apologize that the cuisine for this morning is somewhat inconsistent with the topic for this morning.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.520
In his magisterial work, Golden Doves with Silver Dots,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.100
Professor Faure refers to the writings of the great modern Spanish philosopher

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.980
José Ortega y Gasset, who in his book The Revolt of the Masses

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.040
talks about what he calls the barbarism of specialization.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:47.020
According to Ortega, academic, scientific, and professional specialization

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.920
is an unfortunate characteristic of modern times

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.980
because now individuals know more and more about less and less.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:04.260
It is therefore a great delight to encounter a scholar like Professor Faor

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.700
who is truly an example of a Renaissance person

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:11.060
who is not simply a specialist in one field

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:15.520
but in an extraordinarily wide range of intellectual pursuits

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:24.940
ranging from law to philosophy, from linguistics to Talmud, from literature to theology, from political science to history.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:32.660
The breadth and depth of his scholarship can only evoke the envy of his colleagues and the admiration of his students.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.180
I am pleased to present to you this morning one of the leading Jewish scholars of our time

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:43.660
who will speak to us on a topic close to his heart and mind, the Sepharadi heritage,

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:50.880
which is so intrinsically a part of him and will hopefully become, as a result of his talk, a part of you.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:59.360
I'm honored to present the Ezra Senzibar Visiting Professor at Spertus College for this semester, Professor Jose Faor.

